This is Hidden Brain, I'm Shankar Vedanta. Nearly half a century ago, volunteers in a psychological experiment were shown a slight show of a small red car getting into a crash. Some volunteers were asked, how fast was the car traveling when it passed the yield sign? There was a catch. The original slides showed the car passing a stop sign, not a yield sign. Psychologists Elizabeth Lafterson, her colleagues, later asked volunteers to identify images they had seen before. Some volunteers were shown the earlier slide with a stop sign. Others saw an edited slide where the stop sign was replaced by a yield sign. Volunteers who had been asked the question about the yield sign mistakenly remembered seeing the picture with the yield sign.
这里是《隐藏的大脑》，我是尚卡尔·韦丹塔姆。大约半个世纪前，在一项心理学实验中，志愿者们观看了一段小红车发生碰撞的微型幻灯片。一些志愿者被问到：当汽车经过让行标志时，它开得有多快？这里有个陷阱。原始幻灯片显示的是汽车经过停止标志，而不是让行标志。心理学家伊丽莎白·洛夫图斯和她的同事后来要求志愿者辨认他们以前看过的图片。一些志愿者看到了带有停止标志的早期幻灯片。另一些志愿者看到的则是经过编辑的幻灯片，其中停止标志被替换成了让行标志。那些被问及让行标志问题的志愿者，错误地记成了自己见过带有让行标志的图片。

